// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_twinkey_table.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: the INPUT-REACHABLE half of the twin-key agreement (design §2, P3 Task 6's
// "twin-key desync is impossible by construction"), which lives in TWO guards that must
// fire as a PAIR:
//   * `scene()`'s no-scene-table-under-own ensure (P3 Task 9 guard (2)): an own() layer
//     may not be a scene's ONLY table, because the RUNTIME mode key —
//     `parallax_mode_key()`, the one twin-key half that is not derived from the scene at
//     comptime — ORs the config's two HEADER table words and cannot see the bands. Both
//     header words null with a per-layer table live = runtime answers per-cell while the
//     lowering answered per-line: the desync itself, reachable through the FRONT door.
//   * `scene_caps()`'s CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE implication pin: because `ensure` is
//     non-aborting, the refused scene still folds — to $0020 alone — and the pin that
//     $0020 implies CAP_DEFORM + CAP_PER_LINE fires in its own words. The pair is the
//     R1-Task-9 band() shape exactly (see poison_scene_own_flat.emp): constructor refuses,
//     fold backstops, and WHICH of the two went quiet matters.
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "attaches NO plane-shared table on either plane" — the
// constructor's, so a count of 2 that kept only the fold's would fail on the fragment.
//
// WHY THE OTHER HALF OF "the twin-key agreement (Task 6)" HAS NO ROW HERE, MEASURED:
// Task 6's one new ensure — scene_caps()'s CAP_ANCHORS-implies-CAP_PER_LINE pin — cannot
// be driven red by ANY input, back door included: both bits derive from the same
// `sc_anchor` field through the same `scene_anchor_ch()` accessor (arm 2 of the forcer
// and the `anchored` fold are the same predicate), so no authored value can separate
// them. Measured 2026-08-22 in this worktree: a `Scene{ .. }` back-door anchored scene
// folds to exactly $0009 — see poison_scene_twinkey_anchor.emp, the permanent witness of
// that measurement, and the plan Task 15 DONE block for the booking (the pin's own
// red-first was Task 6's arm-neutering, recorded at the ensure).
//
// TWO FIXTURES, ONE AUTHORED FIELD APART:
//
//   FIXTURE A — one layer carrying `deform: Own(0, 3, 15, 0, 1)` in a scene that ALSO
//               attaches a plane-shared BG table. The legal own() shape: the layer
//               overrides the scene's table, the header words stay non-null, both key
//               twins answer per-line. Folds to the hand-derived $0025
//               (CAP_PER_LINE $0001 | CAP_DEFORM $0004 | CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE $0020)
//               and that fold is the MEASURED passing half.
//   FIXTURE B — byte-for-byte fixture A with `deform_bg:` REMOVED. The own() table is
//               now the scene's only one: scene() refuses it (diagnostic 1), and the
//               fold — $0020 with neither $0004 nor $0001 — trips the implication pin
//               (diagnostic 2).
//
// Expected `[Error]` count is 2, and the pair IS the assertion: a 1 that kept the
// constructor's means the fold's backstop went dead (the implication is once again
// asserted only in a comment); a 1 that kept the fold's fails the fragment too, and it
// would mean the runtime-facing refusal — the guard that actually keeps the header words
// non-null — stopped firing. A 3 means fixture A stopped being legal.
//
// THE TABLE LABELS ARE 0 — variant-discriminated guards, payload-free poisons (see
// poison_scene_own_caps.emp). Own(0, 3, 15, 0, 1): shift_a 3 live, shift_b 15, phase 0,
// speed 1 — one live shift, so layer()'s own-flat guard stays quiet and the ONLY thing
// wrong with fixture B is the missing scene-level table.
//
// THE GLOB IMPORTS ARE THE AUTHOR'S OWN SPELLING — see poison_scene_grid.emp's header.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_twinkey_table

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

// FIXTURE A — own() OVERRIDING a scene-shared table: the legal shape.
const POISON_TK_SCENE_A: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2,
                    deform: SceneDeform.Own(0, 3, 15, 0, 1)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15,
    deform_bg: SceneDeform.Shared(0, 1))

// FIXTURE B — byte-for-byte fixture A, the scene-shared table removed.
const POISON_TK_SCENE_B: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2,
                    deform: SceneDeform.Own(0, 3, 15, 0, 1)),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(),
              no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer(), no_layer() ],
    count: 1, v_factor: 15)

// ---- THE PASSING HALF (must stay green, and is MEASURED) ----
//   $0001 CAP_PER_LINE          the scene-level BG table is forcer arm 1
//   $0004 CAP_DEFORM            a table exists and the own layer's shift_a (3) is live
//   $0020 CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE the own() ref itself
const POISON_TK_FOLDED_A = fold_caps([POISON_TK_SCENE_A])
ensure(POISON_TK_FOLDED_A == $0025,
       "poison_scene_twinkey_table: FIXTURE A folds to {POISON_TK_FOLDED_A}, not the hand-derived 37 ($0025 = CAP_PER_LINE | CAP_DEFORM | CAP_MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE) — an own() layer OVER a scene-shared table is the legal shape, and if it stopped folding all three bits the failing half below no longer isolates the missing header table")

// ---- THE FAILING HALF — the fold is what reaches the implication pin ----
// $0020 alone: the own() ref raises MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE, and with no scene-level table
// there is no has_table for CAP_DEFORM and no forcer arm for CAP_PER_LINE.
const POISON_TK_FOLDED_B = fold_caps([POISON_TK_SCENE_B])
ensure(POISON_TK_FOLDED_B == $0020,
       "poison_scene_twinkey_table: FIXTURE B folds to {POISON_TK_FOLDED_B}, not $0020 — the desync fixture stopped folding to the bare MULTI_DEFORM_TABLE bit, so the two expected diagnostics no longer prove the constructor guard and the implication pin both saw it")
